src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol:initiateWithdraw|class=C22|High|For a pool leg recorded as the ETH sentinel, tokens[i].checkApprove(manager, exitBalances[i]) is a documented no-op for ETH and manager.initiateWithdraw is invoked with no msg.value, so the manager books a withdraw request denominated in exitBalances[i] units of its own ERC-20 yield token while the vault still physically holds that value as native ETH — the escrow branch of convertToAssets then prices the position off a request that has no tokens behind it (double-counting the native ETH the vault kept), letting an unprivileged borrower over-borrow against it.|src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol|<work>/notional/zone-hunt-out/verify/gates/14_src_single_sided_lp_AbstractSingleSidedLP_sol_initiateWithdraw/aux.sol
